# GAIA backend configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. Every value here is optional — GAIA works with an
# empty file, and the settings that matter to day-to-day use live in the app's
# Settings screen instead.
#
# NEVER commit a real `.env`. It is listed in .gitignore.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The recommended place for an API key is the app itself: Settings → AI & Models
# stores it in your operating system's keyring. Set it here only if you prefer
# environment configuration (a server, a container, a shared dev box).
#
# An environment variable takes precedence over a key stored in the keyring.

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where GAIA keeps conversations, settings, logs and backups. Defaults to the
# platform application-data directory:
#   Linux    ~/.local/share/GAIA
#   macOS    ~/Library/Application Support/GAIA
#   Windows  %LOCALAPPDATA%\GAIA

# GAIA_DATA_DIR=/path/to/gaia-data

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GAIA binds to loopback only. Do not expose it on a public interface: there is
# no authentication layer, because it is a single-user desktop application.

# GAIA_HOST=127.0.0.1
# GAIA_PORT=8756
# GAIA_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Extra origins allowed to call the API, comma separated. Only needed for
# unusual development setups.
# GAIA_EXTRA_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Testing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exposes a mock provider that returns canned text. It is NOT a language model
# and exists so the test-suite can run offline. Leave this off in normal use.

# GAIA_ENABLE_MOCK_PROVIDER=0
